fix(qt): load qwebchannel.js again on Qt WebEngine 6.140

Qt WebEngine 6.140 made qrc a local scheme (qtwebengine 8e460f8089b9,
"Make 'qrc' a local scheme", QTBUG-148477), so a page from a remote
scheme can no longer load qrc resources. The UI is served by the daemon
over https and loads qrc:///qtwebchannel/qwebchannel.js, which is now
refused. window.ipc is never set and loadFinished is never sent. With
Start in tray on, the window keeps WA_DontShowOnScreen for good, and
the tray, a second launch and showInstance all show a window that is
never drawn. Every other call from the UI to the app fails the same way,
so settings such as Start in tray and the zoom cannot load or save.

qrc is registered before QApplication as a secure, CORS-enabled scheme,
the part of Qt's documented 6.140 restore that a script loaded by an
https page needs. LocalAccessAllowed only widens what a qrc document may
load, and the app renders none.

Measured on a J316c MacBook Pro (M1 Max) and a Ryzen 9 9950X3D, Qt
6.12.0 with Qt WebEngine 6.140.0-rc. Unpatched: "Not allowed to load
local resource: qrc:///qtwebchannel/qwebchannel.js", and neither
"Initialized closed to system tray." nor "Initialized open window." is
ever logged. Patched: the script loads and the matching line is logged
about a second after the UI.

--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <QLoggingCategory>
 #include <QStandardPaths>
 #include <QTranslator>
+#include <QWebEngineUrlScheme>
 #include <optional>

 #include "connections.h"
@@ -131,6 +132,9 @@
   // Standard Qt Paths:
   // https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qstandardpaths.html
   // settings: ~/.config/{app_id}/{app_id}.conf
+  QWebEngineUrlScheme qrcScheme("qrc");
+  qrcScheme.setFlags(QWebEngineUrlScheme::SecureScheme | QWebEngineUrlScheme::CorsEnabled);
+  QWebEngineUrlScheme::registerScheme(qrcScheme);
   const QApplication a(argc, argv);

   // Qt supplies its own strings for standard dialog buttons (Cancel, Back, Next, OK).
